{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"idling-amaranth-antelope","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context / Problem\nNothing prevents a future doc or script from re-teaching a removed verb, and nothing asserts that the hint registry's replacements are themselves live commands. Cites are on origin/main 2e81cb9767c1.\n\n## Approach\nNew `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_removed_cli_verbs_heldout.py` modelled on `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_bridge_vocabulary_stale_heldout.py:25-66`: (a) for every key in `_help_route._REMOVED_SPELLINGS`: `route_for(key) is None`; `main([key])` exits 2 and stderr has `invalid choice`, the key, and the hint; the hint's first token after `rebar ` is a live top-level route (and for `store ...` a member of `STORE_ROUTES`); (b) a `git ls-files` scan of `docs/ AGENTS.md CONTRIBUTING.md README.md templates/ examples/ src/rebar/_guides/ scripts/ .github/` for `rebar <old>` with the frozen-history prefixes excluded and a whole-file allowlist (`docs/release-notes.md`, `CHANGELOG.md`, `docs/exit-codes.md`, `docs/adr/`, `src/rebar/_cli/_help_route.py`, this test). Extend `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_help_overview_coverage.py` to assert no `help/<old>.txt` artifact survives.\n\n## Scope\n`tests/interfaces/contracts/test_removed_cli_verbs_heldout.py` (new), `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_help_overview_coverage.py`. Out of scope: all source and docs.\n\n## Testing\nThe test fails when run against the store-group story's tree with the docs story reverted (proving it bites) and passes on the docs story's tree; `make verify`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The test is parametrized over the dict with no hard-coded copy of the list.\n- [ ] The scan is proven red-then-green as above (the commit message records both runs).\n- [ ] The test runs in the `ubuntu-latest, py3.13` selection (`not integration and not external`) with no marker beyond the contracts tier.\n- [ ] `make verify` exits 0.","id":"2183-fa68-d48f-42fe","parent_id":"e045-84a5-e545-4f46","priority":2,"tags":["complexity-reduction","breaking-pass-4"],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Held-out test: removed CLI spellings never return to a teaching surface and every hint names a live command"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788806443045238480,"uuid":"70548e30-b620-4a9e-8479-7827b8edf18c"}